      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T18:45:03Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the successful anchor receipt and full call trace, calldata, the helper deployment transaction, archive-node runtimes, the commit-pinned reproduction, two technical incident analyses, and the reported campaign loss. The trace is 0x8ca8... -> Transit router 0x8785... -> helper 0x0b472... callBytes(bytes) -> transfer proxy 0xed1af... claimTokens(...) -> token transferFrom(...). The attacker-controlled callBytes payload names 0xed1af... as its call target and supplies claimTokens calldata containing the token, an approved user, the attacker recipient 0x75f2..., and the amount. The defect-executing artifact is therefore the callBytes helper, not the transfer proxy previously recorded as a proxy target. Helper 0x0b472... was directly created by 0xfab7... in transaction 0x7d83... at block 11986216:300. Its 6,123-byte runtime hashes to 0xb2fa...cabe at deployment and immediately before the exploit; the apparent DELEGATECALL byte is inside trailing compiler metadata, not executable code. Numen and SharkTeam support the approximately $21 million gross cross-chain campaign total."
    }
